    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/hyphessobrycon_cyanotaenia_lapis_tetra_en/",
      "html": "<p>This tetra was introduced under the name \"Inpaichthys sp. Lapislazuli\" in February 2002 by Mrs. Glaser-Dreyer (Aquarium Glaser GmbH). On the (Japanese) internet it is called Lapis tetra. It was imported in a bigger number of pieces without exact declaration of place of discovery.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/hyphessobrycon_cyanotaenia_lapis_tetra_en/",
      "html": "<p>Origin: Brazil.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/hyphessobrycon_cyanotaenia_lapis_tetra_en/",
      "html": "<p>They are almost always moving, very voracious and peaceful; the males are constantly busy with fights for their territory among themselves.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/hyphessobrycon_cyanotaenia_lapis_tetra_en/",
      "html": "<p>The males grow to at least 4 cm and are far more colourful and stronger, with a lengthened dorsal and anal fin, than the lighter females, which are only approx. 3.5 cm long.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/hyphessobrycon_cyanotaenia_lapis_tetra_en/",
      "html": "<p>The breeding was a success for the authors.</p>"
    }
